      "sequence_position": 13,
      "problem": "If $[a]_{n}$ denotes the residue class containing all integers congruent to $a$ modulo $n,$ then $[-26]_{6}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We have $[a]_{6}=[b]_{6}$ if \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6).\n$$\n\nThe residue class $[-26]_{6}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $-26$ modulo $6.$ \n\nWe can find an alternative representation for this residue class as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[-26]_{6} & =\\{x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡-26\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)\\} \\\\  & =\\{x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡(-5)\\cdot 6+4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)\\} \\\\  & =\\{x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡(-5)\\cdot 0+4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)\\} \\\\  & =\\{x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)\\} \\\\  & =[4]_{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
